WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.259
Hey everyone it's Abbey Sharp, welcome to
Abbey's Kitchen. Today I'm dedicating our

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:09.420
video to a very controversial nutrition
topic - artificial sweeteners. Now I get

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.799
asked a lot of questions about
sweeteners - are they safe? Are they better

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.760
then sugar? Are they natural or just a
bunch of chemicals? I have a lot of

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.439
ground to cover here, but I want to focus
on some of the major reasons why people

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:27.090
may use artificial sweeteners and what
the research says about their impact on

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.750
your health. Now before we get into
things of course my general disclaimer

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.620
that all the information in this video
is for entertainment and education

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:37.980
purposes only and you should always
speak to your health care provider about

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.030
your unique healthcare needs.
I also want a flag that I will be

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.329
sharing my own personal experience with
artificial sweeteners at some point

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:50.700
which is not in any way a reason for you
to change your own personal habits.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.289
So, first of all, what are artificial
sweeteners? Now when people say

00:00:55.289 --> 00:01:00.390
"artificial sweeteners" they're actually
talking about extremely low-calorie

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:05.580
sweeteners that are a heck of a lot
sweeter per gram than your typical sugar

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.500
or honey. A more accurate name would be
"non-nutritive sweeteners" or "low-calorie

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.820
sweeteners" depending, of course, on which one you're referring to. But I will

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.000
probably just keep saying artificial
sweeteners most often in this video since

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.330
that is the colloquial term. Now
artificial sweeteners have a very

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.189
similar shape as sugar molecules, so when
they fit on a sweetness receptor found

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:31.049
on your taste buds of your tongue your
body detects it as having a sweet taste.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.040
Having said that, while they may taste
similar, their structure is different

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.210
enough that your body cannot break them
down to yield energy from them. Hence why

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.049
they provide zero or very few calories.
Now there are currently eight

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:47.759
non-nutritive or low-calorie sweeteners
that have been approved by the FDA and

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:53.520
these include -  aspartame aka
nutrasweet or equal, Asulfame Potassium

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.119
aka Sunnett or Sweet One, Monk Fruit
Extract aka Nectrese or PureLo,

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:07.200
Neotame, aka Newtame, Saccharin aka Sweet N' Low or Sugar Twin, Stevia aka Truvia or

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.879
A Sweet Leaf, and Sucralose aka Splenda.
There are also low calorie sugar

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:15.159
substitutes like sugar alcohols which are either found in nature

00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:19.540
or are processed from other sugars.
Generally, you can identify a sugar

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:25.480
alcohol by looking for words that end in "-ol" but a few common sugar alcohols that

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.250
you see in things like gums, gummies,
mints, and other foods include things

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:36.430
like xylitol, erythritol, sorbitol, and
maltitol. Now, people were pretty excited

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.540
when the artificial sweeteners started
to really become popular back in the

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.970
1950s. And, honestly, I don't blame them. If
you had a choice to either consume a can

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:51.159
of soda containing 150 calories, mostly
from sugar, or consume a can of diet soda

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:55.569
with artificial sweeteners containing
zero calories and zero grams of sugar,

00:02:55.569 --> 00:02:59.889
it's a no-brainer which one you're gonna
choose. But of course, in today's wellness

00:02:59.889 --> 00:03:05.109
driven culture, there's definitely been a
lot of necessary skepticism that this

00:03:05.109 --> 00:03:09.159
might just be too good to be true. So
let's talk about some of the new

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:14.200
emerging concerns that some experts have
with artificial sweeteners. Number one -

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:19.180
sweeteners cause cancer. So this one we
can kind of wipe off the table pretty

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.949
damn fast. In contrast to popular belief,
it is pretty clear that artificial

00:03:23.949 --> 00:03:28.540
sweeteners do not cause cancer. Back in
the 1970s, it was suggested that

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:33.040
artificial sweeteners increased one's
risk of bladder cancer. However since

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.269
then, there has been countless human
studies that have found no link

00:03:37.269 --> 00:03:41.290
whatsoever. I'm not going to elaborate on
this one any further because the

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:45.699
research is pretty hard to debate. So
let's move on to some more controversial

00:03:45.699 --> 00:03:49.870
and complicated subjects. Number two -
artificial sweeteners may impair

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:54.489
glucose metabolism and cause insulin
resistance. So one of the biggest reasons

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:58.720
that artificial sweeteners and sugar
substitutes were actually developed in

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.040
the first place, was to help individuals
living with diabetes. Once they

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.479
discovered that these sweeteners did not
have an effect on blood sugar levels the

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:10.900
same way that sugar would, they were
instantly recommended to people with

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.549
diabetes so that they could still enjoy
that flavor of sweetness without worrying

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:19.199
about those spikes in their blood sugar
levels. According to most research,

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:24.250
artificial sweeteners do not raise blood
sugar levels in the short-term. However,

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:28.420
other research has found that when no calorie beverages were consumed at breakfast

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.510
participants experienced a large spike
in blood sugar levels after lunch. This

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:37.010
spike in blood sugar from no-calorie
beverages ended up being about the same

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.680
result
when participants consumed real sugar

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.150
beverages. It's also important to note
however that this was a relatively small

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.350
study and we definitely need more
research in this area to refute this

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:53.270
generally agreed upon belief that these
options may be better for short-term

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:58.370
glycemic control than actual sugar.
Having said that, there is also the

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.300
emerging concern that artificial
sweeteners may actually put people at

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:07.490
risk for certain metabolic diseases.
Specifically, one study by the American

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.810
Diabetes Association found that the
daily consumption of diet drinks

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:19.190
increased the risk of metabolic syndrome
by 36% and type-2 diabetes by 67%. While

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:23.000
those numbers do sound really alarming,
it's important to note that these

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.850
results are observational so for now we
can only establish an association not

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:32.870
causality. In other words, it's very
likely that these individuals were

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:37.190
drinking diet pop because they had or
were at risk of metabolic syndrome or

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.920
diabetes.
There was also, however, a small

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.210
experimental study done in 2014 which
demonstrated that the intake of

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:48.890
sucralose and saccharine, two common
artificial sweeteners, did increase blood

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:52.550
glucose concentrations. After finding
that the sweeteners caused glucose

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:57.140
intolerance in mice, they let seven
healthy volunteers consume artificial

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:02.030
sweeteners for one week. After seven days,
four of the seven individuals developed

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:06.140
poor glycemic responses compared to the
first few days after consuming these

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:11.660
sweeteners possibly suggesting that an
individual's glycemic response may

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:16.940
worsen after regular consumption of
artificial sweeteners. Again, this isn't a

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:21.470
great study so please do take it with a
grain of salt until we have more robust

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:25.880
research to really back it up.
Also, these findings have been refuted by

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:30.290
a number of studies so it is hard to
fully explain the relationship if there

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:34.940
is one but it is believed that some
artificial sweeteners may alter our gut

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:39.410
microbiome which I'm gonna be discussing
in more detail in just a minute. Bottom

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.320
line,
the large body of research in this area

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.340
is largely observational, meaning we
really don't know if the diet soda

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:51.199
causes diabetes and other metabolic
conditions or if it's simply that people

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:56.389
who are at risk of these conditions tend
to drink more diet soda and consume more

00:06:56.389 --> 00:06:59.690
other artificial sweeteners. But let's look
at claim number three -

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:03.800
artificial sweeteners make you eat more.
Now, with artificial sweeteners you're

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:07.790
getting the sweetness without the
calories making it easy for you to trim

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:12.050
calories and potentially lose weight
without losing out on the flavor that

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:16.400
you love. In fact, research has found that
artificial sweeteners may be an

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.270
effective strategy for cutting back on
sugar sweetened beverages. But what is

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:25.910
the net result of that? Well, some experts
are concerned that it's not that easy to

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:30.889
trick your body and because of that lack
of nutritive value you actually would

00:07:30.889 --> 00:07:35.389
need to eat more of the food to feel
satisfied. One animal study had fruit

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:40.760
flies fed a sugar-free diet or a diet
filled with sugar for five or more days.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:46.250
The flies on the sugar-free diet
consumed 30% more calories than the

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.720
flies fed the sugar-containing diet. Once
the sweetener sucralose was removed from

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.130
their diet, their calorie consumption
actually normalized. This was also shown

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:59.030
in a mice study with the same researchers
where the mice were fed a sucralose diet

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:02.479
for seven days and their food
consumption increased by whopping 50%.

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:08.090
Now, let's reiterate that this is animal
research and we don't have a lot of

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:13.130
human studies to really back it up but
one possible explanation for why we may

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:18.050
eat more may be that our brain is not
registering the sweetness as satiating

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:22.310
so your brain realizes that you need to
eat more. When we actually eat something

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.340
sugary,
it activates a food reward pathway in

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:29.750
our brain so that we feel good and we
feel satisfied. Evidence suggests that

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.800
artificial sweeteners don't activate
that same pathway so we don't feel

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:38.240
satisfied and we may even trigger
cravings and the desire to eat more food.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.709
This has led researchers to believe that
sweet foods may need to be coupled with

00:08:42.709 --> 00:08:46.100
calories
for us to feel full and satisfied.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.120
So when we disrupt that balance between
consuming sweet foods without any

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:53.270
calories, we may be interfering with our
appetite

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:57.770
and energy regulation controls.
Having said all of that, a lot of the

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:02.120
current research on humans refutes this
theory and has actually found that

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:07.250
participants tend to report less hunger
and consume fewer calories after eating

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:12.020
artificially sweetened foods. In fact, one
2014 meta-analysis found that

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:16.430
substituting regular calorie foods with
low-calorie sweetener foods yielded

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:20.660
modest weight loss in participants. This
is often being refuted by observational

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.930
studies that have found a link between
consuming artificially sweetened

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:28.700
beverages and higher body weights. So for
example, in the San Antonio Heart study

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:33.440
participants who drank more than 21 diet
drinks per week were twice as likely to

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:38.690
become overweight or obese as people who did not drink diet soda. However, again,

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:43.880
this research in this area is varied and
the observational studies don't really

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:48.200
tell us what comes first - the higher
weight which encourages people to maybe

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:53.750
choose diet food or diet pop, or the
other way around. We also know that there

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:58.700
may be some strong psychological reasons
you're drawn to eat more or more

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.960
"unhealthy" options when you choose an
artificially sweetened beverage.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:07.970
Also known as the "diet coke effect". You know - I'll have a supersize fry and a diet

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:12.440
coke please. Often when people have a
diet product, they either consume more of

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:17.000
the diet food than they usually would or they eat something with higher calories to

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.410
compensate for the lack of satisfaction
from the diet product. One 2015 study

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.550
examined the "health halo effect" which
refers to the act of overestimating the

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:30.560
healthfulness of a food based on a
single claim like low-fat or sugar-free.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:34.370
The study found that when individuals
thought a product was "healthy" they

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:38.990
actually tended to eat more, exercise
less, and were less likely to take care

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:42.500
of their health. Bottom line - I don't
think that artificial sweeteners should

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.250
be relied upon for weight loss and if
you're consuming that much sugar that

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.750
this one thing is making a significant
dent in your overall caloric intake, I

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:55.490
would way rather you find ways to just
adjust your sweetness tolerance, which

00:10:55.490 --> 00:11:00.470
I'm going to be speaking to next. Claim
number 4 - artificial sweeteners increase

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.790
your tolerance for sweetness. So there is
no denying that artificial sweeteners

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.300
are
pretty sweet and because of that there

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:12.320
is some concern that it may actually
change the way we taste and perceive

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:16.550
sweetness in food. to give you a little
bit more perspective, some of these

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:22.220
sweeteners range from about 180 to
13,000 times sweeter than actual sugar.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:26.690
That's a lot! The concern is that if a
person routinely uses artificial

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:31.940
sweeteners, their tolerance for sweetness
may increase and they may find that over

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:36.980
time sweet foods just don't taste sweet
enough. Fruit may not taste sweet, and

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:42.020
vegetables become completely appalling
unless deep-fried and tossed in a sticky

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:45.440
sauce. They may find themselves
increasing their intake of artificial

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:50.630
sweeteners because hey their calorie
free or turning to more sugary foods to

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:55.100
satisfy that sweet tooth while being
turned off completely from naturally

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.600
flavorful nourishing food. While research
in this area is still lacking, there was

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.980
a small survey conducted back in 2015
that found when people cut out sugar

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:09.140
temporarily from their diet their taste
preferences changed by reducing their

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:13.610
desire for overly sweet foods. The same
could potentially be true for artificial

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:18.020
sweeteners. Bottom line, we definitely
need more research on this but I mean

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:21.200
you guys tell me in the comments if this
is something that you've experienced or

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.970
not. I know that when I was consuming a
lot of diet coke in my late teens, this

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:31.310
definitely happened to me and I am
shocked at how sweet I used to like my

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:34.550
coffee and my breakfast foods.
But of course, I'm totally interested in

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.480
hearing your experiences too so
absolutely leave me your thoughts. Now,

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:42.120
claim number 5 - artificial sweeteners cause digestive woes.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:46.250
One of the common issues people
have with some sugar substitutes and

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:49.970
artificial sweeteners is that they may
cause digestive issues. This is

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:55.040
particularly true for sugar alcohols aka
sweeteners like sorbitol,l maltitol,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:13:00.860
mannitol, xylitol lactitol, sorbitol,
etc. Which are really notorious for

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:06.200
causing gas, bloating, and pretty serious
diarrhea. Like in some cases, it's been

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:12.560
described as "napalm in your ass". Why did I say like that? In some cases, it's

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.970
been described as napalm for your bowels.
Now to give you a better idea,

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:20.980
just check out the
Amazon reviews of the sugar-free Haribo

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:25.360
gummies which was made with lycasin
which is a syrup made from maltitol

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:29.920
which is a sugar alcohol. I mean these
were literally used as pranks to keep

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:34.690
your unsuspecting siblings locked in the
bathroom as they cried at the same

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:40.380
time. It was pretty bad. So why do these
particular sweeteners trigger these

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:46.209
not-so-sexy effects? Well, sugar alcohols
are a type of FODMAP aka short-chain

00:13:46.209 --> 00:13:49.810
carbohydrates that are poorly absorbed
in the small intestine. For more

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:53.410
information on FODMAPs you can check out
my video right here. But instead of being

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:58.420
broken down, they actually ferment in the
large intestines leading to some of

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:03.850
those undesirable digestive woes. But
what about the new popular sugar alcohol

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:08.110
based sweetener that promotes none of
these traditional unpleasant side

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:12.940
effects? Let's talk for a hot minute
about Swerve. Now Swerve is becoming

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:18.040
known as the "ultimate sugar replacement"
because it has zero calories, zero net

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:23.140
carbs, and it's even certified non-GMO, if thats something that matters to you.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:28.149
Now Swerve is made from all natural ingredients and contains erythritol, oligo saccharides,

00:14:28.149 --> 00:14:32.500
and natural flavor. Erythritol is a
little different from some other sugar

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:36.940
alcohols because most of it gets absorbed
into the bloodstream before it reaches

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:41.260
the colon, which means it is less likely
that you'll experience digestive issues.

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:45.579
That being said, some research has found
that very large doses of

00:14:45.579 --> 00:14:51.339
erythritol, around 75 grams which is
equivalent to about 2/3 of a cup so a

00:14:51.339 --> 00:14:57.399
lot, was associated with bloating and
diarrhea in 60% of people. We also don't

00:14:57.399 --> 00:15:02.350
really know the impact in individuals
with IBS or very sensitive guts, so again,

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:07.240
this may be an individual thing. As for
other artificial sweeteners, like

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.620
aspartame, saccharine, and a sulfate
potassium,

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:15.190
these are best tolerated by our
digestive systems because they can

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:20.019
easily pass through our system without
many issues for most people. Natural

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:24.399
low-calorie sweeteners, like stevia and
monk fruit extract, also don't tend to

00:15:24.399 --> 00:15:29.020
cause digestive issues. Just keep in mind
that some natural sweeteners are offered

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:31.630
in a blend with other sugar alcohols and
sweeteners

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:37.180
that may cause digestive discomfort. So
always check the package just to be sure.

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:42.610
Bottom line, most sweeteners have no
known effect on bloating, gas, and

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:47.380
diarrhea for most people but if you are
sensitive you may want to limit their

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:52.600
use. And claim six - artificial sweeteners
mess with our gut microbiome. We now know

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:56.470
that our microbiome is involved with
everything from immunity, weight

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:01.090
regulation, mental health, and so much
more. And that it's pretty much the

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:06.130
epicenter of our overall health so
personally I believe in fueling it the

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:10.990
best that we can. As previously discussed
when we talked about insulin and glucose

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:15.490
metabolism levels, there is a lot of
speculation around the impact that

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:20.320
artificial sweeteners may have on our
gut microbiome. According to a 2018 mouse

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:24.070
study, when the gut of the mouse was
exposed to a relatively new sweetener,

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:28.960
Neotame, for four weeks the diversity of
the gut microbiome declined. The same

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.680
effect was found in a 2014 study where
saccharin, sucralose, and aspartame

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:38.050
altered the guts of both mice and humans
while increasing the risk of glucose

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:42.010
intolerance. In the human trial in this
study, researchers found that the gut

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:45.730
bacteria changed in participants after
they consumed non-caloric artificial

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:49.270
sweeteners. More specifically, they found
that the artificial sweeteners led to

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:53.530
the presence of Enterobacteriaceae and Deltaproteobacteria, which are

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:57.670
responsible for a variety of human
diseases. While that's how scary, research

00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:01.660
has found that different people's gut
bacteria could respond differently to

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:07.000
sweeteners, so clearly this research is
still in its early stages. Bottom line, I

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.360
really think that we do need more
studies in this area and I'm actually

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:14.680
quite confident that we will see it.
There is such a huge interest in the gut

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:19.329
microbiome, in general, seeing that it has
such a huge role to play in so many

00:17:19.329 --> 00:17:25.150
aspects of our health. So what we do know
so far is that they likely are safe, but

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:29.590
if you are at all concerned until we do
have more quality research on a larger

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:34.990
population, this particular point right
here in my opinion may be the most

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:39.880
legitimate reason to cut back. But what
about the so-called "natural" sweeteners

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:43.210
on the market? Are they any better for us
than

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:47.320
man-made ones because they come from
nature? So I'm mainly referring to

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:51.580
sweeteners made with things like Stevia,
yacon syrup, and monk fruit. Now when it

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:55.510
comes to these natural sweeteners and
their safety and benefits, the reality is

00:17:55.510 --> 00:18:00.460
we don't have nearly as much research on
these sweeteners as we do with a lot of

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:04.600
the traditional ones. While some early
evidence suggests a stevia may help to

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:09.279
reduce blood pressure in some
populations, it's often also grouped in

00:18:09.279 --> 00:18:12.880
with other artificial sweeteners when
discussing a lot of the negative side

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:17.140
effects or concerns that we've already
discussed. So for example, one review

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.260
found that stevia could potentially
interfere with the concentration of good

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:24.730
gut bacteria. Another study with 30 men
found that participants ate more later

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:28.570
on in the day after consuming a Stevia
sweet drink compared to participants

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:32.679
that consumed sugar sweetened beverages.
The bottom line on Stevia is that, in

00:18:32.679 --> 00:18:38.260
moderation, it does not seem to pose any
significant side effects. However, like

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:43.360
anything in excess, it may be unsafe. So
the recommendation is to not consume

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:48.190
more than four milligrams per kilogram
of body weight in one day, which would be

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:52.990
equivalent to about nine packets per day.
As for monk fruit, one study did not

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:57.399
find any differences between those who
consumed aspartame compared with monk

00:18:57.399 --> 00:19:01.899
fruit or Stevia, suggesting none of the
low-calorie sweeteners, not the natural

00:19:01.899 --> 00:19:06.429
ones or the artificial ones, affected
total energy intake, blood glucose, or

00:19:06.429 --> 00:19:10.179
insulin levels. Aside from that, since
monk fruit is relatively new to the

00:19:10.179 --> 00:19:14.590
sweetener market, we just don't have that
many studies examining its effects. And

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:18.850
then finally there's the trendy and a
harder to find low-calorie option,

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:25.750
yacon syrup, which while natural, has been
known to cause gas, diarrhea, nausea and

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:30.429
other digestive discomfort. One study
found that 10 grams of fructans per day,

00:19:30.429 --> 00:19:36.159
which is about 4 to 5 tablespoons of
yacon syrup, resulted in digestive issues

00:19:36.159 --> 00:19:40.870
for participants. The reason for this is
because yacon syrup contains FODMAPs

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:44.980
called fructuans, so if you're already
dealing with a sensitive gut you may

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:48.580
want to refrain from this particular
sweetener. Otherwise, I recommend sticking

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:53.710
to a small serving, about one gram per
day, to see how it makes you feel. I also

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.530
want to mention that the majority of
Stevia products

00:19:56.530 --> 00:20:03.220
marketed as "natural" are actually usually
blends, meaning it's not even pure stevia.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:07.590
So for example, Truvia contains a blend
of erythritol and stevia leaf extract,

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:13.180
Whole Earth contains a blend of monk
fruit and stevia, and Sugar Like contains

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:17.470
a blend of erythritol and monk fruit. I
also want to tell you quickly about my

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:21.280
personal experience with sweeteners and
how I manage my intake of sweet things

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:25.570
now. Back when I was struggling with
orthorexia and super afraid of sugar, I

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:31.480
drank like 4 to 6 diet cokes a day. I
also put like three splendas in my

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:35.800
coffee and probably would have one or
two of those. I was never really allowing

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:41.500
myself any true real sweetness in my
life, so I had to get my hit from all of

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:45.910
these calorie-free drinks. When I started
to eat a balanced diet again, including

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:50.860
some sweets, I slowly stopped wanting
that diet coke. Then, when I got pregnant

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:54.670
for the first time, I was completely
turned off sweet things and I stopped

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:59.680
using any sweetener in my coffee. And now
if I even have a sip of Diet Coke or a

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.750
little bit of Splenda or sugar in my
coffee,

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:07.450
I am so repulsed by the excess sweetness.
I've also found that now fruits and

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:13.600
vegetables taste so much more flavorful
and naturally sweet to me, so I don't

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:16.000
know if that's just me but definitely
leave me a comment below if that's

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.200
happened to you when you've cut back on
diet coke or or added sweetener to your

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:24.970
coffee. Bottom bottom line here folk,s
based on the current research out there,

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:29.740
artifical sweeteners are not considered
"dangerous" to our health or necessarily

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:33.940
to be completely feared. But they're not
necessarily benign for everyone when

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:38.410
consumed regularly or in large amounts. I
also want to note that it's not

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:42.130
necessarily recommended that pregnant
women consume a large amount of these

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:45.430
sweeteners because they can also
displace a lot of really nutritious and

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:50.110
nourishing food in the diet as well. The
reality is, we really just don't have

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:54.190
enough research to understand some of
the mechanisms behind artificial

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:58.150
sweeteners and we don't have enough
long-term studies to see what they're

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:03.910
lasting impact is. What I can say is that,
whatever you decide to choose, try to use

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:09.580
it in moderation. So whether that's white
sugar, or honey, or Splenda, or stevia,

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:14.169
whatever it is, just try to be mindful
about the portion sizes in general. And

00:22:14.169 --> 00:22:17.649
if your reliance on low-calorie
sweeteners is causing you to increase

00:22:17.649 --> 00:22:22.059
your use of sweet things in general,
that's when I would say it may be time

00:22:22.059 --> 00:22:26.139
for a switch. Having said that, if your
use of low-calorie sweeteners has helped

00:22:26.139 --> 00:22:31.269
you cut back on sugary foods, then I say
there's no harm. This very likely may be

00:22:31.269 --> 00:22:36.039
an individual thing. We will probably be
back here in like a year discussing this

00:22:36.039 --> 00:22:40.570
topic again because I think the evidence
is just mounting, but until then if you

00:22:40.570 --> 00:22:44.289
like this video be sure to give it a
thumbs up, leave me a comment below on

00:22:44.289 --> 00:22:48.820
why you do use or do not use artificial
sweeteners, subscribe to the channel and

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:53.129
I will see you next time on Abbey's
Kitchen. Bye!

